\begin{align*}
\text{Total females who listen} &= \text{Total who listen} - \text{Males who listen} \\
&= 130 - 62 \\
&= 68 \\
\end{align*}

We know that the table shows that there are 150 total people surveyed, and 102 of them are females. Using the total number of females and the number of males who don't listen, we can find out how many females don't listen to the station:

